<title>BRAZIL: Brazil January foreign reserves $57.8 bln.</title>
<headline>Brazil January foreign reserves $57.8 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's net foreign reserves in January stood at $57.8 billion, or $58.9 billion according to the international liquidity concept, which includes accounts receivable, the Central Bank said Friday.</p>
<p>December net foreign reserves were of $59.03 billion, or $60.1 billion according to the international liquidity concept.</p>
<p>((--Adrian Dickson, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 248 5410))</p>
